bench/bench
bench/coeff
bench/gen
#
# The rate experiments build one bench per factor - bench-os4, bench192 -
# and shoot-loop.py writes its wavs and its page beside them.  All of
# them are throwaways of a particular afternoon.
#
bench/bench-*
bench/bench[0-9]*
#
# bench.reference_bench() builds an old commit's bench in a throwaway
# worktree here, cached by commit id, which is what --model takes.
# 'git worktree prune' after deleting one.
#
bench/ref/
spice-cache/
distortion-shootout.html
distortion-shootout-*.wav
#
# compare-spice.py --waves, and whatever was drawn beside it while
# chasing one afternoon's defect.
#
waves-*.png
#
# Bench captures: a few megabytes of samples belonging to one pedal on
# one evening.  capture-rat.py makes them and draw-rat.py reads them;
# neither the samples nor the figures drawn from them are committed.
# The figures that are on the page are, as PNGs - a page has to read
# correctly from a clone, and the scripts say how to remake the rest.
#
rat-*.json
rat-*.html
rat-*.wav
figures/
